name 'thinking-critically-about-ai-postassessment-q9_2026-pilot'

question 'A student gets feedback from a peer that their Credibility Guide is "too hard to understand." The student then asks an AI tool for feedback, and the AI says the guide is "clearly written and easy to follow." How should the student respond?'

wrong 'Accept the AI\'s feedback, since it has processed more writing than the peer and is more reliable.'
wrong 'Reject both sources of feedback and trust their own original judgment.'
right 'Take the peer\'s feedback seriously, since the peer represents the actual target audience, and consider that the AI may not accurately assess readability for the students this guide is meant for.'
wrong 'Ask a second AI tool for feedback, and go with whichever AI agrees with the peer.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lessons 6, 9
